%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0605eb6777c11a4468d9fd35aa1e3c94, type: 3}
  m_Name: BuiltInFormatterRules
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: TimboJimbo.Localization.Editor::AdditionalProjectContextBlocks
  ContextBlocks:
  - _title: Pluralization Formatter
    _body: "# Localization Pluralization Guidelines\r\n\r\nTranslate strings using
      our custom C# plural formatter. You MUST adapt the pluralization to match the
      **target language's** grammatical rules (CLDR), overriding the source language's
      structure.\r\n\r\n## 1. Syntax & Supported Keys\r\n- **Format:** `{index:plural|key=value|key=value}`\r\n-
      **Keys:** `zero`, `one`, `two`, `few`, `many`, `other` (Case-insensitive. If
      used, maintain this exact order. `other` is mandatory if the formatter is used).\r\n\r\n###
      Target Language Key Matrix (CRITICAL)\r\nOnly use the keys explicitly listed
      for your target language code. Do NOT use keys omitted from its list:\r\n-
      **No Plurals (Only use `other`):** `zh`, `ja`, `ko`, `vi`, `id`, `ms`, `th`,
      `km`, `lo`, `my`\r\n- **Only `one`, `other`:** `fr`, `hi`, `bn`, `gu`, `mr`,
      `pa`, `fa`\r\n- **Only `one`, `few`, `many`, `other`:** `ru`, `uk`, `be`, `sr`,
      `hr`, `bs`, `pl` *(0 maps to `many` in Slavic and `other` in Polish. Never
      use `zero` or `two` here!)*\r\n- **Only `one`, `few`, `other`:** `cs`, `sk`,
      `ro`, `lt`\r\n- **Only `zero`, `one`, `other`:** `lv`\r\n- **Full Set (`zero`,
      `one`, `two`, `few`, `many`, `other`):** `ar`\r\n- **Default (Only `zero`,
      `one`, `other`):** `en`, `de`, `es`, `pt`, `it`, `nl`, `sv`, `da`, `no`, `el`,
      `bg`, `et`, `fi`, `hu`\r\n\r\n## 2. CRITICAL TRANSLATION BEHAVIORS\r\n\r\n**A.
      The \"No-Plural\" Bypass (Asian/Turkic Languages)**\r\nIf the target language
      uses a static noun regardless of the number (e.g., Turkish, Japanese, Chinese),
      **DELETE the plural block entirely.**\r\n- *Source:* `You have {0:N0} {0:plural|one=message|other=messages}.`\r\n-
      *Target (Turkish):* `{0:N0} yeni mesaj\u0131n var.`\r\n\r\n**B. Surgical Scoping
      & Number Omission (Complex Languages)**\r\nIf the target language implies the
      quantity in the singular or dual word form (e.g., Arabic), you must delete
      the external number and move it *inside* the block using `[#]`. \r\n**CRUCIAL:**
      Keep the block wrapped *only* around the specific noun/adjective. Leave all
      surrounding static text outside the block.\r\n- *Source:* `There are {0:N0}
      new {0:plural|one=car|other=cars} for sale!`\r\n- *Target (Arabic):* `\u0647\u0646\u0627\u0643
      {0:plural|zero=0 \u0633\u064A\u0627\u0631\u0627\u062A \u062C\u062F\u064A\u062F\u0629|one=\u0633\u064A\u0627\u0631\u0629
      \u062C\u062F\u064A\u062F\u0629 \u0648\u0627\u062D\u062F\u0629|two=\u0633\u064A\u0627\u0631\u062A\u0627\u0646
      \u062C\u062F\u064A\u062F\u062A\u0627\u0646|few=[#:N0] \u0633\u064A\u0627\u0631\u0627\u062A
      \u062C\u062F\u064A\u062F\u0629|many=[#:N0] \u0633\u064A\u0627\u0631\u0629|other=[#:N0]
      \u0633\u064A\u0627\u0631\u0629} \u0644\u0644\u0628\u064A\u0639!`\r\n*(Note:
      The external `{0:N0}` is removed, the digit is omitted for 1 and 2, `[#:N0]`
      is used for the rest, and \"There are/for sale!\" remains outside the block).*\r\n\r\n**C.
      Grammatical Shift**\r\nYou are free to move the plural block away from the
      noun and onto a verb or adjective if the target grammar dictates it (e.g.,
      Hindi verbs).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Cheat Sheet Examples\r\n* **French (Basic):**
      `Vous avez {0:N0} {0:plural|one=nouveau message|other=nouveaux messages}.`\r\n*
      **Turkish (Bypass):** `Bug\xFCn {0:N0} elma ald\u0131m.` *(Formatter dropped
      entirely)*\r\n* **Hindi (Shift):** `\u092C\u093F\u0915\u094D\u0930\u0940 \u0915\u0947
      \u0932\u093F\u090F {0:N0} \u0915\u093E\u0930 \u0909\u092A\u0932\u092C\u094D\u0927
      {0:plural|one=\u0939\u0948|other=\u0939\u0948\u0902}!` *(Formatter moved to
      the verb)*\r\n* **Polish (Surgical):** `Znalaz\u0142e\u015B {0:plural|one=[#:N0]
      monet\u0119|few=[#:N0] monety|many=[#:N0] monet|other=[#:N0] monety}!` *(Numbers
      moved inside, cases applied. Polish does NOT support or use zero/two).*"
  - _title: Map Formatter
    _body: "# Localization Map Formatter Guidelines\r\n\r\nTranslate strings using
      our custom C# map formatter. The map formatter swaps in specific text based
      on an exact match with the input variable. You MUST adapt the output text to
      the target language while leaving the programmatic keys completely untouched.\r\n\r\n##
      1. Syntax & Structure\r\n- **Format:** `{index:map|key1=value1|key2=value2|other=fallback}`\r\n-
      **Alias:** `m` can be used instead of `map` (e.g., `{0:m|...}`).\r\n- **Rule:**
      Every entry MUST have a key (`key=value`), except for `other=...` which is
      the fallback. Unkeyed entries will break the string.\r\n- **Valid Keys:** Exact
      strings (case-insensitive), bools (`true`/`false`), or literal numbers (`0`,
      `42`, etc. using invariant culture).\r\n\r\n## 2. CRITICAL TRANSLATION BEHAVIORS\r\n\r\n**A.
      NEVER Translate the Keys (Left Side of `=`)**\r\nKeys are runtime values. Translating
      them will break the code. Translate ONLY the value on the right side of the
      `=`.\r\n- *Source:* `{0:map|red=Red|blue=Blue|other=Unknown color}`\r\n- *Target
      (French):* `{0:map|red=Rouge|blue=Bleu|other=Couleur inconnue}` *(Notice 'red'
      and 'blue' remain in English).*\r\n\r\n**B. Preserve Every Key (No Dropping/Merging)**\r\nThe
      C# code expects a specific set of possible inputs. Do not drop, add, or combine
      keys.\r\n\r\n**C. Surgical Scoping & Grammatical Shifting**\r\nYou may freely
      move surrounding static text in and out of the block to match target grammar,
      as long as the block stays wrapped around the variable part.\r\n- *Source:*
      `Status: {0:map|true=Online|false=Offline}.`\r\n- *Target (Japanese):* `\u30B9\u30C6\u30FC\u30BF\u30B9:
      {0:map|true=\u30AA\u30F3\u30E9\u30A4\u30F3|false=\u30AA\u30D5\u30E9\u30A4\u30F3}\u3002`\r\n\r\n**D.
      Map vs. Plural**\r\nUse `map` for arbitrary discrete values (colors, states,
      specific numeric callouts like \"1=snake eyes\"). Use the `plural` formatter
      if the choice is driven by grammatical number rules.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Cheat
      Sheet Examples\r\n* **Bool Toggle:** `{0:map|true=Enabled|false=Disabled}`\r\n*
      **String Enum (Spanish):** `{0:m|gold=Oro|silver=Plata|bronze=Bronce|other=Sin
      medalla}` *(Keys untouched!)*\r\n* **Numeric Callout (Surgical):** `You rolled
      a {0:map|1=1 \u2014 snake eyes!|20=20 \u2014 critical hit!|other=[#].}`"
  - _title: Query Formatter
    _body: "# Localization Query Formatter Guidelines\r\n\r\nTranslate strings using
      our custom C# query formatter. The query formatter acts like an if/else chain,
      picking a string based on conditional logic evaluated top-to-bottom. \r\n\r\n##
      1. Syntax & Structure\r\n- **Format:** `{index:query|cond1=value1|cond2=value2|defaultValue}`\r\n-
      **Alias:** `q` can be used instead of `query` (e.g., `{0:q|...}`).\r\n- **The
      Default Value:** The fallback has NO equals sign (`=`). There can only be one
      default, and it MUST be placed at the very end.\r\n\r\n## 2. Supported Conditions
      (The Left Side)\r\n- **Numbers:** Operators `<, <=, >, >=, =/==`, or a bare
      number for exact match (e.g., `<=10`, `42`). Uses invariant culture (always
      `.` for decimals).\r\n- **Time/Dates:** Operator + duration + suffix `ms, s,
      m, h, d`. (e.g., `<-1d` is past, `>30m` is future).\r\n- **Strings/Bools:**
      Exact matches (case-insensitive).\r\n\r\n## 3. CRITICAL TRANSLATION BEHAVIORS\r\n\r\n**A.
      NEVER Translate the Conditions (Left Side of `=`)**\r\nThe left side is code,
      not text. Do not localize the conditions, numbers, operators, or time suffixes.
      Translate ONLY the right side and the default value.\r\n- *Source:* `{0:query|<=0=none|<10=a
      few|>=1000=heaps|[#:N0] items}`\r\n- *Target (French):* `{0:query|<=0=aucun|<10=quelques-uns|>=1000=des
      tas|[#:N0] articles}`\r\n\r\n**B. Strict Ordering (Do Not Sort)**\r\nEntries
      are evaluated top-to-bottom. The first match wins. Reordering the keys will
      break the logic. Keep the default at the end.\r\n\r\n**C. Time Suffixes are
      Code**\r\nSuffixes like `ms, s, m, h, d` are programmatic. Do not translate
      them into your target language (e.g., do not change `d` to `j` for French *jours*).\r\n-
      *Target (German):* `{0:query|<-1d=gestern oder fr\xFCher|<0=heute, fr\xFCher|>1d=in
      mehr als einem Tag|bald}`\r\n\r\n**D. Surgical Scoping & Grammatical Shifting**\r\nIf
      the target language naturally includes the digit inside the chosen phrase,
      delete the outer base parameter (`{0}`) and move it inside using `[#]`. Move
      the block onto verbs or adjectives if target grammar demands it.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n##
      Cheat Sheet Examples\r\n* **Numeric Thresholds:** `Score: {0:N0} \u2014 {0:query|<=0=try
      again!|<50=keep going|<90=great!|perfect!}`\r\n* **Relative Time (Spanish):**
      `Visto por \xFAltima vez {0:query|<-7d=hace m\xE1s de una semana|<-1d=hace
      unos d\xEDas|<0=hoy m\xE1s temprano|<1h=en menos de una hora|en el futuro}.`
      *(Conditions untouched!)*\r\n* **Bare Default & Formatting:** `{0:q|0=Empty|<10=Almost
      empty|>=100=Full|[#:N0] / 100}`"
  - _title: Formatter Params
    _body: "## Parameter vs. Internal Placeholder\r\n- `{0}` (or `{1}`, etc.) is
      the base parameter used *outside* the format block.\r\n- `[#]` is the internal
      placeholder used *inside* the format block to reference that same active number.\r\n-
      **NO NESTED BRACES `{}`:** Internal placeholders MUST use square brackets `[]`
      (e.g., `[#]`, `[#:N0]`).\r\n  - **CRITICAL:** Standard curly brackets `{}`
      are strictly FORBIDDEN inside custom formatters (`plural`, `map`, `query`).
      \r\n  - **Do NOT nest or cross-reference other variables** like `{1}` or `{2}`
      inside the plural block. If you must output multiple variables, place them
      outside the block entirely.\r\n  - *Invalid (Nested/Cross-referenced):* `{0:plural|one={1}
      apple|other=[#] apples}`\r\n  - *Invalid (Nested self):* `{0:plural|one={[#]}
      apple|other=[#] apples}`\r\n  - *Valid:* `{1} {0:plural|one=apple|other=[#]
      apples}`\r\n- **Formatting:** You can apply basic C# formatting to the internal
      placeholder (e.g., `[#:N0]`) but you can not use `plural`, `map` and `query`
      formatters on the internal placeholder. No nested!\r\n"
